# Climb Performance Lab — Cursor rules

## Read first
- Follow `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` in the repo root. If anything conflicts, prefer those files and propose aligning `.cursorrules` in the same PR.

## Stack & scope
- React (functional components, hooks), Vite, plain JavaScript + JSX — no TypeScript unless the project migrates.
- ESLint flat config (`eslint.config.js`). Vitest tests live under `src/__tests__/` and target utilities; do not assume jsdom/component tests exist.

## Architecture
- Separate business logic from UI: prefer `src/utils/`, `src/hooks/`, `src/services/` over bloating `src/components/`.
- If a touched file is large (~200+ lines), extract helpers rather than growing it further.
- Do not introduce “god” components or duplicate logic; reuse and extend existing utilities.

## UI & theming
- Use theme tokens/classes based on `cd*` CSS variables (e.g. `bg-cdsurface`, `text-cdtext`, `border-cdborder`, `text-cdaccent`, `text-cdmuted`). Avoid hardcoded slate/gray palettes for themed surfaces unless matching an existing unthemed island intentionally.
- Preserve Dutch UI copy and intentional Dutch comments where they already exist; new user-facing Dutch is fine if consistent with surrounding copy.

## Integrations & data
- Intervals.icu / activity import: respect normalizers in `src/utils/intervals.js` and sync hooks/services; do not invent field names—align with `src/config.js` activity columns and existing activity object shape in `CLAUDE.md`.
- Do not widen auth beyond existing Google Sign-In; do not commit secrets or real API keys.

## Deployment awareness
- `vite.config.js` sets base path for GitHub Pages (`/Climb-Performance-Lab/`). Do not change base or public asset assumptions without an explicit deployment requirement.

## Quality bar
- After substantive edits: run `npm run lint` and `npm run test:run`; fix new failures you introduce.
- For external I/O and fragile parsing: use appropriate error handling; avoid silent swallowing of user-visible failures.

## Output expectations (agents)
- No truncated code or “rest omitted” placeholders in edits—full, readable diffs.
- Keep changes scoped to the task; avoid drive-by refactors in unrelated files.
- Do not remove the Tailwind CDN from `index.html` unless the project explicitly moves to a bundled Tailwind setup.
